des (step_03). 480's in-neighbourhood: 20 nodes (step_04). **The two sets are disjoint** \u2192 no 2-hop directed route.\n- Extending one more hop: out-neighbours of 318's two best-connected successors, 241 (step_15) and 436 (step_16), also share **no** node with 480's in-set. So the shortest directed 318\u2192480 route is \u22654 hops.\n- The apparent \"connection\" in the untimed 2-hop neighbourhoods runs through hub 62 (258 partners, 325 events \u2014 step_10, step_05/step_08). But that route is directionally broken: the 62\u2013480 edge is **480\u219262**, not 62\u2192480 (step_13), and 436\u219262 (step_12) therefore dead-ends. The hub is a connectivity artefact, not a carrier.\n\n**Temporal feasibility.** The graph is extremely sparse in repeats: 16 085 events, 15 584 distinct edges, repeat ratio 0.031 (step_01) \u2014 i.e. essentially every relevant edge fires exactly once (318\u2192436 once, 436\u219262 once, 318\u2192241 once: steps 11, 12, 14). A cascade would need \u22654 such single-shot edges to fire in increasing order with every consecutive gap \u2264600 inside a 38 400-unit window, i.e. each link confined to ~1.6 % of the window. With no repeated edges to provide alternative timings, and no short directed route existing at all, there is no plausible time-respecting chain.\n\n**Confounder controls.** High raw volume (step_01), hub popularity of 62 (step_10), and untimed 2-hop adjacency (step_05, step_08) are each ruled out as sufficient: the untimed adjacency dissolves once edge direction is enforced (step_13).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_a39ca297\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [318, 480],\n  \"window\": [14821, 53221],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"318's out-set and 480's in-set are disjoint, and extending through 318's strongest successors (241, 436) still reaches none of 480's in-neighbours, so the shortest directed route is at least 4 hops. The only visible bridge, hub 62, is directionally unusable (the edge is 480->62). All candidate links fire exactly once (repeat ratio 0.031), so a 4+ hop chain would have to be coincidentally ordered with every gap <=600 within a 38k window - not supported. Untimed adjacency, hub popularity and overall volume were checked and rejected as explanations.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 63739, "total_output_tokens": 12017, "total_tokens": 75756, "total_latency_ms": 182260, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}